                  <msItem xml:id="ms_i0">
                     <locus from="2v" to="44v">2v-44v</locus>
                     <textLang xml:lang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s22IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#2v">-2v</locus>سورة بني اسرائيل مكية وهي مائة واحد عشرة ايوة. بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ سُبْحَانَ الَّذِي أَسْرَىٰ بِعَبْدِهِ لَيْلًا مِنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْأَقْصَى الَّذِي بَارَكْنَا حَوْلَهُ<note>17:1</note>
                     </incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#44v">-44v</locus>فَانْطَلَقَا حَتَّى إِذَا لَقِيَا غُلامًا فَقَتَلَهُ قَالَ أَقَتَلْتَ نَفْسًا زَكِيَّةً بِغَيْرِ نَفْسٍ لَقَدْ جِئْتَ شَيْئًا نُكْرًا <note>18:74</note>
                     </explicit>
                     <note>17:1-18:74. Some words are divided into two different lines.
The “ḏāl” is written with the dot inside. Sometimes the catchword is only the first part of the first word in the next page, sometimes there is a repeated word and the catchword is the second word of the next page. 
The name of the scribe appears in mss. 4521D (37r) and 4521X (1v, 45v). The note stating that he is actually the scribe is in 4521X (45v).  </note>
                     <note/>
                  </msItem>
